          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<h1 id=\"demo-2a-heat-islands-at-zet-stops--lisa-hotspot-clustering-with-spatial-ai-oml4py\">Demo 2a: Heat Islands at ZET Stops – LISA Hotspot Clustering with Spatial AI (OML4Py)</h1>\n<p><strong>HrOUG 2026 · Spatial Meets AI</strong> · Which ZET stops need shade first?</p>\n<p>Heat is not spread at random over a city: hot places sit next to hot places. This notebook measures that <strong>spatial dependence</strong> for Zagreb with Spatial AI in Oracle Machine Learning for Python (OML4Py) on Autonomous AI Database, and turns it into a first shortlist of stops that need shade.</p>\n<p>It answers four questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Is surface heat around ZET stops clustered, or randomly spread?</strong> Global Moran's I and its p-value.</li>\n<li><strong>Where are the significant heat islands (high-high) and cool islands (low-low)?</strong> Cool islands are expected at Maksimir, Jarun and the Sava banks.</li>\n<li><strong>Which stops lie in a heat-island cluster?</strong> That gives the first shortlist for shade.</li>\n<li><strong>Which stops are local outliers,</strong> like a hot stop in a cool neighbourhood (high-low)? These are the micro-site problems.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Adapted from the Oracle sample notebook <em>OML4Py Spatial AI Hotspot Clustering</em> (Copyright (c) 2025 Oracle Corporation, <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://oss.oracle.com/licenses/upl/\">The Universal Permissive License (UPL), Version 1.0</a>).</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
        },
