          "%md",
          "",
          "###### Prepare ZET_STOPS",
          "",
          "`ZET_STOPS` holds one row per ZET stop: a GTFS station (`location_type` 1) that groups the platforms of both directions. It comes from the [ZET GTFS schedule](https://zet.hr/gtfs-scheduled/latest):",
          "1. The database downloads the GTFS ZIP into `ZET_GTFS_FILES`.",
          "2. Python reads the ZIP and derives, per station, the transport mode (tram or bus), the number of platforms, and the departures on a weekday.",
          "3. SQL creates `ZET_STOPS` with an `SDO_GEOMETRY` point and a spatial index, and stores the GTFS ids of the hook stops A–D in `TRAM_STATIONS`.",
          "Stops: ZET GTFS (feed version 000396).",
          "",
          "GTFS = General Transit Feed Specification",
          " "
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
