          "results" : [
            {
              "message" : "<h6 id=\"prepare-zet_stops\">Prepare ZET_STOPS</h6>\n<p><code>ZET_STOPS</code> holds one row per ZET stop: a GTFS station (<code>location_type</code> 1) that groups the platforms of both directions. It comes from the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://zet.hr/gtfs-scheduled/latest\">ZET GTFS schedule</a>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The database downloads the GTFS ZIP into <code>ZET_GTFS_FILES</code>.</li>\n<li>Python reads the ZIP and derives, per station, the transport mode (tram or bus), the number of platforms, and the departures on a weekday.</li>\n<li>SQL creates <code>ZET_STOPS</code> with an <code>SDO_GEOMETRY</code> point and a spatial index, and stores the GTFS ids of the hook stops A–D in <code>TRAM_STATIONS</code>.\nStops: ZET GTFS (feed version 000396).</li>\n</ol>\n<p>GTFS = General Transit Feed Specification</p>\n",
              "type" : "HTML"
            }
          ],
          "forms" : "[]"
