          "%md",
          "",
          "###### 1. Is surface heat clustered, or randomly spread?",
          "",
          "The spatial weights define who is a neighbour: every H3 cell and its 6 nearest cells, the ring of hexagons around it. For the stops, the 6 nearest stops.",
          "",
          "Global Moran's I is close to 0 (more precisely, its expected value) when values are spread at random, and positive when similar values sit next to each other. A p-value below 0.05 means the pattern is very unlikely to be random."
        ],
        "selectedVisualization" : "html",
        "visualizationConfig" : null,
        "hideCode" : true,
        "hideResult" : false,
        "hideGutter" : true,
        "hideVizConfig" : false,
